NAME
    sed - apply a bounded line-editing script

SYNOPSIS
    sed [-n] [-e SCRIPT | SCRIPT] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Streams lines from standard input or files. At an interactive prompt
    standard input reads typed lines until Ctrl-D; see man sh. The supported
    scripts are p, d, and s/OLD/NEW/[g], optionally prefixed by one positive
    line number.
    Substitution patterns are literal bytes; & in NEW expands to OLD. The -n
    option suppresses ordinary output. Ranges, regular expressions, captures,
    multiple commands, and in-place editing are not implemented.
